@startuml
' Final architecture based on memento_drawing_documented.cpp (C++20).
title Memento Design Pattern - Drawing Application\nClass architecture (C++20)

top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam classFontSize 16
skinparam classAttributeFontSize 14
skinparam nodesep 100
skinparam ranksep 110
skinparam padding 10
skinparam dpi 160

' Use SVG export for zooming without clipping or loss of detail.
' Keep relationship explanations in the legend, not on connector paths.
' EntryStack, Scope and ShapeIds are diagram-only type abbreviations.


class Drawing <<Originator>> {
    - shapes_ : std::vector<Shape>
    .. Private helpers ..
    - findShapeById(id : int) : Shape*
    - findShapeById(id : int) const : const Shape*
    - mementoContainsShape(memento : const DrawingMemento&, id : int) const : bool
    .. Editing ..
    + addShape(shape : Shape) : void
    + moveShape(id : int, dx : double, dy : double) : void
    + resizeShape(id : int, factor : double) : void
    .. Snapshot and restoration ..
    + save() const : DrawingMemento
    + restore(memento : const DrawingMemento&) : void
    + restoreShape(memento : const DrawingMemento&, id : int) : void
    + restoreShapes(memento : const DrawingMemento&, shapeIds : const ShapeIds&) : void
    + restoreLinkedShapes(memento : const DrawingMemento&, id : int) : void
    .. Read-only operations ..
    + getLinkedShapeIds(id : int) const : std::vector<int>
    + getShape(id : int) const : Shape
    + print() const : void
}

class DrawingMemento <<Memento>> {
    - shapes_ : std::vector<Shape>
    - DrawingMemento(shapes : const std::vector<Shape>&)
}

class DrawingHistory <<Caretaker>> {
    - undoStack_ : std::vector<HistoryEntry>
    - redoStack_ : std::vector<HistoryEntry>
    .. Shared history algorithm ..
    - {static} transfer(drawing : Drawing&, source : EntryStack&, destination : EntryStack&, shapeIds : const Scope&) : void
    .. Public operations ..
    + save(drawing : const Drawing&) : void
    + canUndo() const noexcept : bool
    + canRedo() const noexcept : bool
    + undo(drawing : Drawing&) : void
    + undo(drawing : Drawing&, id : int, mode : RestoreMode) : void
    + redo(drawing : Drawing&) : void
}

class HistoryEntry <<struct>> {
    + memento : DrawingMemento
    + shapeIds : std::optional<std::vector<int>>
}

enum RestoreMode <<enum class>> {
    Full
    Individual
    Linked
}

class Shape <<type alias>> {
    std::variant<Circle, Rectangle>
}

class Circle <<struct>> {
    + id : int
    + x : double
    + y : double
    + radius : double
    + groupId : int
}

class Rectangle <<struct>> {
    + id : int
    + x : double
    + y : double
    + width : double
    + height : double
    + groupId : int
}

class "Shape helpers" as Helpers <<free functions>> {
    + getShapeId(shape : const Shape&) : int
    + getGroupId(shape : const Shape&) : int
}

class "Client / tests" as Client <<free functions>> {
    + makeDrawing() : Drawing
    + testRestoration(mode : RestoreMode, label : const char*) : void
    + testMultipleUndoRedo() : void
    + testFailedLinkedUndo() : void
    + main() : int
}

' Relationships: short, unlabelled connectors prevent label collisions.
' A single composition edge represents both history stacks.
Client ..> Drawing
Client ..> DrawingHistory
Client ..> RestoreMode
DrawingHistory ..> Drawing
DrawingHistory ..> RestoreMode
DrawingHistory *-- "0..*" HistoryEntry
HistoryEntry *-- "1" DrawingMemento
Drawing ..> DrawingMemento
Drawing *-- "0..*" Shape
DrawingMemento *-- "0..*" Shape
Shape ..> Circle
Shape ..> Rectangle
Drawing ..> Helpers
Helpers ..> Shape

legend bottom
  **Relationship key**
  Filled diamond: composition (owned values).
  Dashed arrow: dependency (uses a type or its operations).
  Drawing owns current shapes; DrawingMemento owns saved copies.
  DrawingHistory owns entries in both undoStack_ and redoStack_.
  Each HistoryEntry owns one memento and its restoration scope.
  Drawing creates and restores mementos; it uses the shape helpers.
  Shape depends on its two variant alternatives; helpers use std::visit.
  Client calls Drawing and DrawingHistory and selects RestoreMode.

  **Diagram-only type abbreviations**
  EntryStack = std::vector<HistoryEntry>
  ShapeIds = std::vector<int>
  Scope = std::optional<std::vector<int>>

  **Encapsulation and restoration**
  DrawingMemento stores private snapshots; friend class Drawing
  grants direct access to the Originator, not the Caretaker.
  Group 0 means ungrouped; positive IDs identify linked shapes.
  Collect linked IDs before restoring group membership.
  Validate every selected ID in both states before modification.
  Full restoration uses copy-and-swap.

  **Undo / redo consistency**
  nullopt = full restoration; a vector of IDs = selective restoration.
  Save a checkpoint before an edit; saving clears redo history.
  Push the current state to the opposite stack, restore the source
  snapshot, then consume the source entry. Roll back on failure.
  Selective undo consumes the latest checkpoint, not an arbitrary
  earlier per-shape state. Later undo / redo preserve the exact IDs.
endlegend

' Shape is an alias, not a base class. Helpers and Client are conceptual
' groupings of free functions, not actual C++ classes.
' No inheritance: variant alternatives are type dependencies.
' Group membership is stored by ID; no owning Shape-to-Shape relationship.
' canUndo() and canRedo() are noexcept in the C++ implementation.

@enduml
